{% comment %}
  The product information accordions - four columns in the design, each with a
  heading of its own and a stack of accordion rows under it.

  Shopify section blocks are a flat list, so "rows inside a column" has to be
  expressed some other way. This section does it by position: a `group` block
  starts a column, and every `item` block after it belongs to that column until
  the next `group`. Dragging a row from one column to another in the theme
  editor is then exactly what it looks like - moving it above or below a group
  heading - and no block has to be told which column it lives in.

  (The first version of this section did tell every row its column number, and
  wrapped a group accordion round a row accordion with a script opening and
  closing the outer layer at the breakpoint. The column numbers were miserable
  to set up, so they are gone for good. The two levels are back because the
  design asks for them, but the outer one is a button and a div rather than a
  second <details>, so there is no accordion nested inside an accordion and no
  breakpoint logic: the columns behave the same way at every width.)

  Columns are open on load and stay open without JavaScript - the `is-open`
  class ships in the markup and only collapsing needs the script. So a failed
  or blocked product-page.js costs the shopper the ability to fold a column
  away, not the ability to read it.

  A row can take its text from a product metafield as well as typing it, by
  putting the key in `Metafield key`. The metafield wins on products that have
  one and the typed text stands in on products that do not, so one template can
  serve a catalogue where only some products document, say, their craft
  technique, without the rest of them showing an empty row or none at all.
  Rows with neither a metafield value nor typed text are skipped, a column with
  no surviving rows is skipped, and the section disappears when nothing
  survives at all.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'product-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'product-page.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- liquid
  comment
    The Specification row is built from three fit metafields rather than one
    key, so resolve them up front - the liveness pass and the render loop then
    read the same values instead of asking twice and risking disagreement.
  endcomment
  assign spec_fit = product.metafields.custom.fit.value | default: product.metafields.custom.fit
  assign spec_model = product.metafields.custom.model_details.value | default: product.metafields.custom.model_details
  assign spec_reco = product.metafields.custom.fit_recommendation.value | default: product.metafields.custom.fit_recommendation
  assign has_spec = false
  if spec_fit != blank or spec_model != blank or spec_reco != blank
    assign has_spec = true
  endif

  comment
    Pass 1. One flag per block, in block order:
      'g' a group heading
      '1' an item with something to show
      '0' an item with nothing to show
    Deciding liveness once, here, is what makes the count that gates the
    section, the count that gates each column and the render loop agree by
    construction rather than by three copies of the same condition.
  endcomment
  assign flags = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'group'
      assign flags = flags | append: 'g,'
    elsif block.type == 'spec'
      assign live = false
      if block.settings.heading != blank
        if has_spec or block.settings.content != blank
          assign live = true
        endif
      endif
      if live
        assign flags = flags | append: '1,'
      else
        assign flags = flags | append: '0,'
      endif
    elsif block.type == 'description'
      comment
        The full product description, which the buy box no longer carries - it
        shows custom.short_description there instead. A product with an empty
        description hides the row rather than opening onto nothing.
      endcomment
      assign live = false
      if block.settings.heading != blank and product.description != blank
        assign live = true
      endif
      if live
        assign flags = flags | append: '1,'
      else
        assign flags = flags | append: '0,'
      endif
    elsif block.type == 'contact'
      assign live = false
      if block.settings.heading != blank
        if block.settings.instagram_handle != blank or block.settings.whatsapp_display != blank or block.settings.text != blank
          assign live = true
        endif
      endif
      if live
        assign flags = flags | append: '1,'
      else
        assign flags = flags | append: '0,'
      endif
    else
      assign live = false
      if block.settings.heading != blank
        assign key = block.settings.metafield_key | strip
        assign field = ''
        if key != blank
          assign field = product.metafields.custom[key]
        endif
        comment
          Typed text is a fallback, not an alternative. A row pointed at a
          metafield used to ignore whatever was typed on it and hide itself
          wherever that metafield was empty, so the only way to give a row
          default copy was to give up per-product copy for it entirely.

          Now the metafield wins where a product has one and the typed text
          stands in where it does not, which is the same order
          sections/pdp-why-love.liquid already resolves its columns in. A row
          with neither is still skipped, so "hide what this product has nothing
          to say about" survives - it just means both sources empty rather than
          one.
        endcomment
        comment
          "Metafield only" turns the fallback off for rows the design asks to
          appear only when there is something particular to say - the craft
          technique row, which should be absent on a product with no
          hand-block printing, embroidery, quilting or smocking rather than
          carrying a generic paragraph. It is ignored when no key is set,
          since that would leave the row permanently unreachable.
        endcomment
        assign allow_fallback = true
        if key != blank and block.settings.metafield_only
          assign allow_fallback = false
        endif

        if field != blank
          assign live = true
        elsif allow_fallback and block.settings.content != blank
          assign live = true
        endif
      endif
      if live
        assign flags = flags | append: '1,'
      else
        assign flags = flags | append: '0,'
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  comment
    Comma-delimited rather than one character per block: `split: ''` splitting a
    string into characters is Ruby behaviour this template should not lean on.
    No flag is ever empty, so no interior entry can be dropped, and a trailing
    delimiter is discarded - the list stays the same length as section.blocks.
  endcomment
  assign flag_list = flags | split: ','

  comment
    Pass 2. Which columns survive. A column is identified by the block index of
    its group heading alone - the rows are "everything after it until the next
    group", which both this count and the render loop walk the same way.

    Index -1 stands for a leading column with no heading, used when a merchant
    has left item blocks above the first group. Those rows still render rather
    than silently disappearing.
  endcomment
  assign starts = ''
  if flag_list.size > 0 and flag_list[0] != 'g'
    assign starts = '-1,'
  endif
  for block in section.blocks
    unless block.type == 'group'
      continue
    endunless
    assign starts = starts | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
  endfor
  assign start_list = starts | split: ','

  assign total = 0
  assign live_starts = ''
  for start in start_list
    assign gi = start | plus: 0
    assign found = 0
    for flag in flag_list
      if forloop.index0 <= gi
        continue
      endif
      if flag == 'g'
        break
      endif
      if flag == '1'
        assign found = found | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
    if found > 0
      assign live_starts = live_starts | append: start | append: ','
      assign total = total | plus: found
    endif
  endfor
  assign live_start_list = live_starts | split: ','
-%}

{%- if total > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="pdp-section color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
    style="--pdp-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px; --pdp-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;"
  >
    <div class="pdp-section__inner">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <p class="pdp-eyebrow pdp-info__label">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The column count is the number of columns that survived, not a setting.
        A template with four groups gets four columns; one whose fourth group is
        entirely metafield-driven and empty on this product gets three, at full
        width, rather than three columns and a gap.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="pdp-info__grid{% if live_start_list.size == 1 %} pdp-info__grid--single{% endif %}"
        style="--pdp-info-columns: {{ live_start_list.size }};"
      >
        {%- for start in live_start_list -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign gi = start | plus: 0
            assign group_heading = ''
            assign group_attributes = ''
            if gi >= 0
              assign group_block = section.blocks[gi]
              assign group_heading = group_block.settings.heading
              assign group_attributes = group_block.shopify_attributes
            endif
          -%}
          <pdp-info-group class="pdp-info__group is-open" {{ group_attributes }}>
            {%- if group_heading != blank -%}
              <h3 class="pdp-info__grouprow">
                <button
                  class="pdp-info__grouphead"
                  type="button"
                  aria-expanded="true"
                  data-pdp-group-toggle
                >
                  <span class="pdp-info__grouptitle">{{ group_heading | escape }}</span>
                  {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'caret' -%}
                </button>
              </h3>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="pdp-info__rows">
              {%- assign opened = 0 -%}
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Walk forward from this column's group heading and stop at the
                  next one. `flag_list` decides what shows, so the condition
                  lives in one place - see pass 1.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- if forloop.index0 <= gi -%}
                  {%- continue -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'group' -%}
                  {%- break -%}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if flag_list[forloop.index0] != '1' -%}
                  {%- continue -%}
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- liquid
                  assign key = block.settings.metafield_key | strip
                  assign field = ''
                  if key != blank
                    assign field = product.metafields.custom[key]
                  endif
                -%}
                <details
                  class="pdp-info__item"
                  {% if section.settings.open_first and opened == 0 %}open{% endif %}
                  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
                >
                  <summary>
                    <span class="pdp-info__heading">{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}</span>
                    {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'caret' -%}
                  </summary>
                  <div class="pdp-info__content rte">
                    {%- if block.type == 'spec' -%}
                      {%- if has_spec -%}
                        <ul class="pdp-info__spec">
                          {%- if spec_fit != blank -%}
                            <li>
                              <span class="pdp-info__specterm">
                                {{- block.settings.fit_label | default: 'Fit' | escape -}}
                              </span>
                              <span>{{ spec_fit | escape | newline_to_br }}</span>
                            </li>
                          {%- endif -%}
                          {%- if spec_model != blank -%}
                            <li>
                              <span class="pdp-info__specterm">
                                {{- block.settings.model_label | default: 'Model' | escape -}}
                              </span>
                              <span>{{ spec_model | escape | newline_to_br }}</span>
                            </li>
                          {%- endif -%}
                          {%- if spec_reco != blank -%}
                            <li>
                              <span class="pdp-info__specterm">
                                {{- block.settings.recommendation_label | default: 'Fit tip' | escape -}}
                              </span>
                              <span>{{ spec_reco | escape | newline_to_br }}</span>
                            </li>
                          {%- endif -%}
                        </ul>
                      {%- else -%}
                        {{ block.settings.content }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- elsif block.type == 'description' -%}
                      {{ product.description }}
                    {%- elsif block.type == 'contact' -%}
                      {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
                        <p>{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        Same two links as the buy box's size-help block, and the
                        same reason the wa.me number is a separate digits-only
                        setting: wa.me rejects spaces and plus signs, so the
                        number shown and the number linked cannot be one field.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      <ul class="pdp-info__contact">
                        {%- if block.settings.instagram_handle != blank -%}
                          <li>
                            <a
                              class="pdp-info__contactlink"
                              href="{{ block.settings.instagram_url | default: 'https://instagram.com/' }}"
                              target="_blank"
                              rel="noopener"
                            >
                              {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'instagram' -%}
                              <span>{{ block.settings.instagram_handle | escape }}</span>
                            </a>
                          </li>
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {%- if block.settings.whatsapp_display != blank -%}
                          {%- assign wa = block.settings.whatsapp_number | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-' | strip -%}
                          <li>
                            {%- if wa != blank -%}
                              <a class="pdp-info__contactlink" href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                                {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'whatsapp' -%}
                                <span>{{ block.settings.whatsapp_display | escape }}</span>
                              </a>
                            {%- else -%}
                              <span class="pdp-info__contactlink">
                                {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'whatsapp' -%}
                                <span>{{ block.settings.whatsapp_display | escape }}</span>
                              </span>
                            {%- endif -%}
                          </li>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </ul>
                    {%- elsif field != blank -%}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        A rich text metafield renders its own HTML when output
                        directly. Every other type is a plain string, which has
                        to be escaped and needs its line breaks turned into
                        markup to survive in an HTML context.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      {%- if field.type == 'rich_text_field' -%}
                        {{ field }}
                      {%- else -%}
                        <p>{{ field.value | default: field | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {{ block.settings.content }}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                </details>
                {%- assign opened = opened | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </pdp-info-group>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        "Need any help?" - a panel at the foot of the accordions, not one of
        them.

        It is section settings rather than a block on purpose. A block type
        added at the same time as a template that uses it loses a race with
        Shopify's sync: the template is ingested against whatever schema the
        store has already loaded, and settings it cannot find there are
        dropped. That is what happened to the first version of this - the
        template still carried the block, its settings arrived empty, so the
        row read as "nothing to show" and hid itself. `enable_sticky_media`
        went the same way across all 22 templates. Section settings resolve
        against the schema in this same file, so there is no window to lose.

        Every field falls back to its default, and the panel hides only when
        there is genuinely nothing to show - no title and no way to reach
        anyone.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign help_phone = section.settings.help_phone_display | strip
        assign help_phone_href = section.settings.help_phone_number | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | strip
        assign help_wa = section.settings.help_whatsapp_number | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-' | strip

        assign has_help_contact = false
        if help_phone != blank or section.settings.help_whatsapp_label != blank
          assign has_help_contact = true
        endif

        comment
          Resolved into one flag rather than written as a mixed and/or in the
          tag below. Liquid has no operator precedence and evaluates right to
          left, so `enabled and title or enabled and contact` parses as
          `enabled and (title or (enabled and contact))` - which happens to be
          right here and would stop being right the moment a term moved.
        endcomment
        assign show_help = false
        if section.settings.help_enabled
          if section.settings.help_title != blank or has_help_contact
            assign show_help = true
          endif
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if show_help -%}
        <div class="pdp-info__help">
          <div class="pdp-info__helpcard">
            <div class="pdp-info__helptext">
              {%- if section.settings.help_title != blank -%}
                <p class="pdp-info__helptitle">{{ section.settings.help_title | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if section.settings.help_subtitle != blank -%}
                <p class="pdp-info__helptitle">{{ section.settings.help_subtitle | escape }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

            {%- if has_help_contact -%}
              <ul class="pdp-info__helplinks">
                {%- if help_phone != blank -%}
                  <li>
                    {%- if help_phone_href != blank -%}
                      <a class="pdp-info__helplink" href="tel:{{ help_phone_href }}">
                        {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'phone' -%}
                        <span>{{ help_phone }}</span>
                      </a>
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="pdp-info__helplink">
                        {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'phone' -%}
                        <span>{{ help_phone }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if section.settings.help_whatsapp_label != blank -%}
                  <li>
                    {%- if help_wa != blank -%}
                      <a
                        class="pdp-info__helplink pdp-info__helplink--chat"
                        href="https://wa.me/{{ help_wa }}"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                      >
                        {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'whatsapp' -%}
                        <span>{{ section.settings.help_whatsapp_label | escape }}</span>
                      </a>
                    {%- else -%}
                      <span class="pdp-info__helplink">
                        {%- render 'pdp-icon', icon: 'whatsapp' -%}
                        <span>{{ section.settings.help_whatsapp_label | escape }}</span>
                      </span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              </ul>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if section.settings.help_hours != blank -%}
              <p class="pdp-info__helphours">{{ section.settings.help_hours | escape }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP: Info columns",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "pdp-section-wrapper",
  "max_blocks": 32,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Add a Column heading block to start a column, then Accordion blocks under it. Every accordion belongs to the column heading above it, and the number of columns is however many you add — the design uses four."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Section label",
      "info": "The small label above the columns. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "open_first",
      "label": "Open the first accordion in each column",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "\"Need any help?\" panel"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A panel at the foot of the accordions, not one of them. Clear the title and both contacts to hide it."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "help_enabled",
      "label": "Show the panel",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_title",
      "label": "Line one",
      "default": "Need any help?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_subtitle",
      "label": "Line two",
      "default": "Get in touch."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_phone_display",
      "label": "Phone shown",
      "default": "+91 93197 50031"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_phone_number",
      "label": "Phone for the link",
      "default": "+919319750031",
      "info": "Digits, with the country code. Used for tel: — a plus sign is fine here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_whatsapp_label",
      "label": "WhatsApp link text",
      "default": "Chat"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_whatsapp_number",
      "label": "WhatsApp number",
      "default": "919319750031",
      "info": "Digits only — wa.me rejects spaces and plus signs."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "help_hours",
      "label": "Hours",
      "default": "Mon–Sat 9:30 AM to 5:30 PM (IST)"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.colors.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.colors.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.padding.section_padding_heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_top",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding.padding_bottom",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "group",
      "name": "Column heading",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Product details",
          "info": "Shown uppercase. Every accordion below this block, until the next Column heading, sits in this column."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "name": "Accordion",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Fabric"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "Per-product text (optional)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "metafield_key",
          "label": "Metafield key",
          "info": "Key inside the `custom` namespace, e.g. `craft_technique`. Products that have this metafield show it instead of the text above; products that do not fall back to the text above. Leave both empty to hide this row."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "metafield_only",
          "label": "Hide this row when the metafield is empty",
          "default": false,
          "info": "Turns the fallback text off, so the row appears only on products that have the metafield. Use it for rows that should be absent rather than generic — the craft technique, for instance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spec",
      "name": "Specification",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Built from three product metafields — custom.fit, custom.model_details and custom.fit_recommendation. The row hides itself on products where all three are empty, unless you type fallback text below."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Specification"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "fit_label",
          "label": "Label for custom.fit",
          "default": "Fit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "model_label",
          "label": "Label for custom.model_details",
          "default": "Model"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "recommendation_label",
          "label": "Label for custom.fit_recommendation",
          "default": "Fit tip"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Fallback text",
          "info": "Shown only on products where all three metafields are empty. Leave empty to hide the row there instead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "description",
      "name": "Accordion: product description",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Shows the product's own description. The buy box shows the short intro from custom.short_description instead, so this is where the full copy lives. Hidden on products with no description."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Description"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "contact",
      "name": "Accordion: contact / size help",
      "limit": 1,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Need help choosing your size?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Intro line",
          "default": "Chat with us on Instagram or Whatsapp"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "Instagram"
        },
